module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_restore_reopens_a_slot_the_host_never_provisioned

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BelowCeiling, FoundBelowTheLadder, FoundOnRung, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, MechanicallyPreventable }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

data a_restore_reopens_a_slot_the_host_never_provisioned: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_restore_reopens_a_slot_the_host_never_provisioned" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead {
    found_at: FoundBelowTheLadder,
    standing: BelowCeiling {
      current: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable },
      ceiling: MechanicallyPreventable,
      blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt,
      trigger_capability: "a re-admission that cannot express starting a unit the host cannot run: gunbc.runner.runner_host_cap_bracket::release_slot_over reads the slot tree standing for the unit it is about to release and, where the tree is proven absent and the unit proven not instantiated, takes the first install BEFORE the enable and start, and where the tree is absent while the unit is instantiated, refuses that unit by name instead of starting it -- the start being issued only over a tree the same pass proved present, SUFFICIENT FOR the withdraw witness to red the merge path if a restore ever starts a recorded unit whose tree it has not established",
    },
  },

  receipts: [
    "**a control that re-admits a unit from a record of what was taken out, without asking whether the host can run that unit at all.** INVALID STATE: a host reported admitting, its unit unmasked, enabled, loaded and with a process, while the directory the unit runs from does not exist -- so the slot can never register and never takes work, and the model's own population line counts it as open. HARM: the operator is told the host is back and it is not; and because the unit is now active with no tree, every later pass reaches a state that REFUSES rather than repairs, so the host is stuck out of service by a control that reported success. The refusal is not local either: an unsettled actuation on one slot holds the host-wide cap convergence, so the slots that DO work keep running under caps the model has already decided to change.",
    "SPECIMEN, 2026-11-19, srv3. srv3-06 and srv3-07 carried no slot tree on the host: the baseline read (run 44454553045, 04:15:53Z) had them LoadState=masked, admission=masked, run=stopped, no registration, and nothing in the model held them masked -- they are the two ex-fabric execution slots per host that gunbc.design_ruling::srv3_srv4_fabric_slots_serve_ci (PR #16137) returned to GitHub Actions, and no provisioning pass had ever built their trees under /opt/actions-runner. The bracket then treated their mask as a withdrawal of working slots: run 44595938568 recorded 'state=withdrawn units=actions-runner@srv3-01.service..srv3-13.service record=written' -- 06 and 07 among them -- and run 44603235081 tried to bring them back and refused: 'actuation actions-runner@srv3-06.service REFUSED step=readback not loaded, enabled, cleanly active with a main process after one settle: ActiveState=; activating; result=; exit-code; MainPID=; main=none', 07 identically. Its retry, run 44606128349, caught both units inside a restart window, read 'active' and reported 'state=admitting units=actions-runner@srv3-01.service..srv3-13.service record=cleared'. The next read (run 44609820213, 20:54:26Z) said what they actually were: 'slot-tree unit=actions-runner@srv3-06.service REFUSED slot tree absent while active' and 'slot-registration unit=srv3-06 UNREADABLE the host holds no readable current registration for srv3-06', with the drain reading for the same unit 'admission=open run=listener-idle'.",
    "THE STATE THEN CLOSES ITSELF OFF FROM REPAIR, AND HOLDS THE HOST WITH IT. run 44621007740 (21:39:46Z) brought the other eleven kept slots to 'restarted-and-live-cgroup-read-back' after writing 20-fleet-width.conf and 40-fleet-high.conf, refused 06 and 07 at 'step=slot-tree slot tree absent while active', and left the host 'slots observed=21 effective=0 retired-as-declared=8' with all thirteen kept slots reading 'ALLOCATION-NOT-EFFECTIVE CPUQuotaPerSecUSec=5s want=9000000us'. Two legs, both host-wide, gate on those two units being settled: gunbc.runner.runner_host_file_converge::runner_host_cpu_dropin_gate filters 60-fleet-cpu.conf out of the plan while any actuation is unsettled -- so the per-slot CPU quota the model has already derived is never written, and the file is still 'content=differs action=write' on srv3 where srv4's copy reads 'content=identical' -- and the shadow removal of gunbc.runner.runner_host_file_converge::runner_host_control_shadow_paths refuses while gunbc.runner.runner_host_file_converge::runner_host_cap_phase_settled is false, so the stale 50-MemoryMax.conf, 50-MemoryHigh.conf, 50-MemorySwapMax.conf and 50-TasksMax.conf under /etc and /run/systemd/system.control stay exactly where the older width left them.",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: the restore's re-admission fold (gunbc.runner.runner_host_cap_bracket::release_slot_over, shared with the cap release) asks only whether the unit is masked, and then issues unmask, enable, start; it never reads the slot tree, and the restore mode has no tree leg at all -- so the mode whose whole job is re-admission is the one route that turns 'masked and unprovisioned' into 'active and unprovisioned'. Once the unit is instantiated with no tree, gunbc.runner.runner_host_file_converge::runner_slot_instantiation puts it in SlotInstantiationAnomalous, and gunbc.runner.runner_host_file_converge::runner_slot_tree_step refuses that arm rather than building under a live unit -- a refusal pinned by the claim a_never_instantiated_slot_queues_its_first_install_without_draining in gunbc.test.claim.runner.deploy_slot_account_witness. The arm that DOES build, the first install queued for a slot proven not instantiated, lives inside the activation leg that gunbc.recurring_failure_mode::a_withdrawal_undone_by_the_next_converge made hold on a withdrawn record: so withdrawing the host to get the two units proven stopped buys a record that holds the install too, and restoring without the install puts the anomaly back. No sequence of the existing modes repairs the state, which is what makes the class a repair-route gap rather than a mis-ordered run.",
    "RUNG NOW: mitigatable -- the anomaly is typed, located per unit and countable, and the host-wide gates that hang on it are visible in the same receipt that reports 'effective=0', so an operator can see the host is not back; nothing prevents the state from being entered. CEILING: mechanically preventable once re-admission cannot issue a start except over a tree the same pass established -- present, or absent-and-proven-not-instantiated and then installed -- because the harm needs the start, not the mask, and the unprovisioned slot sitting masked is merely an unmet population, loudly readable. The climb is unbuilt rather than blocked: the install function already exists (gunbc.runner.runner_host_file_converge::rebuild_runner_slot_tree, the same call the converge's queued-first-install arm uses after the unit files and the reload), and the reading that discriminates the two treeless states is already produced (gunbc.runner.runner_host_file_converge::runner_slot_instantiation). What is missing is the restore reaching for either, and a witness that reds a restore which starts a recorded unit whose tree it has not established.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
